ommits/adbf4eaed16bab8f51248806a27ca64c5ac4f29b"}],"sha":"44098b937ece4a9bd1645da9fb1076e1531f23a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/microfrontends/commits/44098b937ece4a9bd1645da9fb1076e1531f23a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/8329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel","id":35613825,"login":"vercel[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MzU2MTM4MjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/microfrontends/commits/adbf4eaed16bab8f51248806a27ca64c5ac4f29b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-08T22:12:37Z","email":"35613825+vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"vercel[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-08T22:12:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Update React Flight/Next.js RCE vulnerability (#27)\n\n## React Flight / Next.js RCE Advisory Fix\n\n### Summary\nUpdated the Vercel Microfrontends repository to address the React Flight / Next.js RCE advisory by upgrading vulnerable Next.js packages from version 15.5.4 to 15.5.7.\n\n### Vulnerability Analysis\nThe repository is a monorepo containing:\n- The core `@vercel/microfrontends` package (uses Next.js as dev dependency)\n- Multiple Next.js example applications (nextjs-app, nextjs-pages)\n- React Router and single-spa examples (not affected - they don''t use React Flight packages)\n\n**Vulnerable Packages Detected:**\n- `next@15.5.4` found in 5 package.json files\n\n**Not Vulnerable:**\n- The project does NOT use React Flight packages directly (`react-server-dom-webpack`, `react-server-dom-parcel`, or `react-server-dom-turbopack`)\n- React and React DOM are only present in non-Next.js examples and are not affected\n\n### Changes Made\n\n#### Files Modified:\n1. `packages/microfrontends/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7 (dev dependency)\n\n2. `examples/nextjs-app/docs/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n3. `examples/nextjs-app/marketing/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n4. `examples/nextjs-pages/blog/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n5. `examples/nextjs-pages/dashboard/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n#### Lockfile Updated:\n- `pnpm-lock.yaml` updated to resolve `next@15.5.7` and its dependencies\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n**Upgrade Rationale:**\n- According to the advisory, Next.js 15.5.x requires upgrade to 15.5.7\n- This patch version includes the security fix for the React Flight RCE vulnerability\n- No major version bumps were performed (all were 15.x)\n- React and React DOM versions remain unchanged as they are not directly vulnerable\n\n**Build Verification:**\n- Core package (`@vercel/microfrontends`) builds successfully\n- One of the example Next.js projects (`nextjs-pages-dashboard`) builds successfully with `next@15.5.7`\n- No application logic changes were required - only dependency versions updated\n\n**Environment Setup:**\n- Used `pnpm install` to update dependencies and lockfile\n- Verified that the lockfile correctly resolves to `next@15.5.7` in all contexts\n- Confirmed all peer dependencies and resolution work correctly\n\n### Files NOT Modified\n- Root `package.json` - does not contain Next.js as a dependency\n- Non-Next.js examples - no React Flight or Next.js dependencies present\n- React and React DOM versions - maintained as-is per advisory guidance (Next.js will provide correct patched versions)\n\n### Testing\n- Package resolution: ✓ Successful\n- Build test (nextjs-pages-dashboard): ✓ Successful\n- Lockfile generation: ✓ Successful\n\n### Compliance\nThis fix strictly adheres to the advisory requirements:\n- Only Next.js packages were modified (15.x versions)\n- No unnecessary dependency changes were made\n- React versions were NOT manually updated (Next.js handles this)\n- No projects using React Flight packages required changes (not in use in this repo)\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"14a1d1d3cc2dafdf470810d1972e58004ea4f4f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/microfrontends/git/trees/14a1d1d3cc2dafdf470810d1972e58004ea4f4f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/microfrontends/git/commits/adbf4eaed16bab8f51248806a27ca64c5ac4f29b","verification":{"payload":"tree 14a1d1d3cc2dafdf470810d1972e58004ea4f4f1\nparent 62d24b1f7991e730449821e0af2a249bef118bcd\nauthor vercel[bot] <35613825+vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1765231957 -0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1765231957 -0800\n\nUpdate React Flight/Next.js RCE vulnerability (#27)\n\n## React Flight / Next.js RCE Advisory Fix\n\n### Summary\nUpdated the Vercel Microfrontends repository to address the React Flight / Next.js RCE advisory by upgrading vulnerable Next.js packages from version 15.5.4 to 15.5.7.\n\n### Vulnerability Analysis\nThe repository is a monorepo containing:\n- The core `@vercel/microfrontends` package (uses Next.js as dev dependency)\n- Multiple Next.js example applications (nextjs-app, nextjs-pages)\n- React Router and single-spa examples (not affected - they don''t use React Flight packages)\n\n**Vulnerable Packages Detected:**\n- `next@15.5.4` found in 5 package.json files\n\n**Not Vulnerable:**\n- The project does NOT use React Flight packages directly (`react-server-dom-webpack`, `react-server-dom-parcel`, or `react-server-dom-turbopack`)\n- React and React DOM are only present in non-Next.js examples and are not affected\n\n### Changes Made\n\n#### Files Modified:\n1. `packages/microfrontends/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7 (dev dependency)\n\n2. `examples/nextjs-app/docs/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n3. `examples/nextjs-app/marketing/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n4. `examples/nextjs-pages/blog/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n5. `examples/nextjs-pages/dashboard/package.json`\n   - Upgraded `next` from 15.5.4 to 15.5.7\n\n#### Lockfile Updated:\n- `pnpm-lock.yaml` updated to resolve `next@15.5.7` and its dependencies\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n**Upgrade Rationale:**\n- According to the advisory, Next.js 15.5.x requires upgrade to 15.5.7\n- This patch version includes the security fix for the React Flight RCE vulnerability\n- No major version bumps were performed (all were 15.x)\n- React and React DOM versions remain unchanged as they are not directly vulnerable\n\n**Build Verification:**\n- Core package (`@vercel/microfrontends`) builds successfully\n- One of the example Next.js projects (`nextjs-pages-dashboard`) builds successfully with `next@15.5.7`\n- No application logic changes were required - only dependency versions updated\n\n**Environment Setup:**\n- Used `pnpm install` to update dependencies and lockfile\n- Verified that the lockfile correctly resolves to `next@15.5.7` in all contexts\n- Confirmed all peer dependencies and resolution work correctly\n\n### Files NOT Modified\n- Root `package.json` - does not contain Next.js as a dependency\n- Non-Next.js examples - no React Flight or Next.js dependencies present\n- React and React DOM 